FlowGraph
Copyright (c) 2026 Abdolmanaf Mehrabi Sisakht

FlowGraph is made of parts under two licenses. Each source file names its license in an SPDX line at its top
(SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT or GPL-3.0-only), and each part has a LICENSE file of its own.

MIT (LICENSES/MIT.txt) - the runtime, usable in any application, closed source included:
  Core/                    FlowGraphCore: types, scripts, compiler, interpreter, built-in nodes
  EditorCore/              what the editors share without a user interface (the document, running and debugging)
  Apps/Flow/               flow, the command line runner
  Plugins/FileSystem/      the FileSystem plugin (also an example of a plugin)
  Examples/MakeExamples.cpp, Examples/Scripts/
  Tests/ (except Tests/EditorTests.cpp), Tools/, cmake/, the build files

GPL-3.0-only (LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt) - the editors (the Qt editor because it is built on KDDockWidgets, which
is licensed under GPL-2.0-only or GPL-3.0-only):
  GLEditor/                FlowGraphGLEditor, the editor on GLWidgets
  Apps/Studio/             flowstudio, FlowGraph Studio
  Editor/                  FlowGraphEditor (the ScriptEditor library, on Qt), its icons and resources
  Examples/QtStudio/       flowstudio-qt, FlowGraph Studio on the Qt editor library
  Examples/Embedded/       the example of an application that embeds the Qt editor
  Tests/EditorTests.cpp

An application that embeds the editor is a work based on GPL-3.0 code; an application that only uses the
runtime (FlowGraphCore) is not.

Third-party components
  KDDockWidgets   ThirdParty/KDDockWidgets, GPL-2.0-only or GPL-3.0-only (its LICENSE.txt and LICENSES/);
                  linked into the editor only
  GLWidgets       ThirdParty/GLWidgets, MIT (its LICENSE), with what it builds in (SDL3, FreeType, HarfBuzz,
                  SheenBidi, libunibreak, ThorVG, the Vazirmatn font: their licenses in its folder and, in the
                  packages, in share/doc/FlowGraph/GLWidgets); linked into flowstudio only
  Qt              LGPL-3.0 (LICENSES/LGPL-3.0.txt, which supplements LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt); used by the Qt editor
                  only, as shared libraries
The runtime uses only the C++ standard library and the operating system. Its calendar arithmetic
(Core/Source/BuiltinsTime.cpp) follows the date algorithms Howard Hinnant published and donated to the public
domain ("chrono-compatible low-level date algorithms").
